What Is the Acrylonitrile Market?
Acrylonitrile is an organic chemical compound used primarily as a raw material in the manufacture of synthetic fibers, engineering plastics, and other chemical products. It is a key input for polyacrylonitrile fibers, ABS and SAN resins, acrylamide, and nitrile butadiene rubber (NBR).

The market covers acrylonitrile production, sales, pricing, distribution, and consumption across industrial applications and geographical regions. Production technology, feedstock availability, manufacturing capacity, and the performance of downstream industries all influence market conditions.

Because acrylonitrile is toxic and subject to chemical safety requirements, manufacturers must also manage workplace exposure, emissions, storage, transportation, and regulatory compliance.

